<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>A wanderer within the world</l><l>For pleasure ever seeks;</l><l>Be it in body or in mind,</l><l>With vanity it reeks.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>For self I labored day and night,</l><l>My castles built in sand;</l><l>But, praise the Lord, He wrecked them all—</l><l>Much better things He planned.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Once all for self—confused, alone,</l><l>How could I bear the shame?</l><l>But now within the local church</l><l>I’ll never be the same.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>I am a happy member now</l><l>Within the local church.</l><l>A wanderer has found his home</l><l>And ended all his search.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>I was an individualist,</l><l>An island in myself;</l><l>But now the Lord is building me</l><l>With others in Himself.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>I’m drawn together with His own</l><l>In fellowship so sweet.</l><l>I’ve learned from others to receive</l><l>Of Christ whene’er we meet.</l></lg>
<lg label="8."><l>My wanderings have really ceased—</l><l>I’ve found the church, God’s best!</l><l>The secret of my happiness—</l><l>Enjoying God’s own rest!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
